00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.120 align:start position:0%
fire axes just announced a new XCOM  spin-off called chimera squad and it's  changing up the formula in some big ways  here's what you need to know first this  isn't a sequel it's a standalone  spin-off that set five years after XCOM  two humans and aliens are actually  working together but some of Earth's  natives aren't happy about it  chimera squad includes both human and  alien soldiers and they investigate  threats to this new inner species  Alliance each squad member has their own  unique abilities which is a huge  departure from the series customizable  cannon fodder soldiers making random  roles each member also gets their own  turn during combat there isn't one macro  phase for your turn followed by the  enemies every unit has their own place  in the timeline and some of those unique  abilities can manipulate who gets to act  first  you can even stack some of these  abilities together for powerful combo  attacks these combat encounters take  place in discrete locations in a single  city each mission is self-contained with  multiple shifting objectives  you'll start each mission with the new  breach mode which lets you choose your  initial starting point on the map some  of these starting points can only be  used by humans or aliens and where you  begin the mission will change the flow  of your objectives within this is all  leading up to chimera squads biggest  change there is no permit earth if a  squad member goes down they begin  bleeding out if they don't stabilize  within a few turns they'll die which  restarts the mission however game overs  are still possible each mission takes  place in a different sector with their  own levels of unrest if you let one  sector get too unruly the chaos will  overtake the entire city  chimera squad sounds like a pretty big  departure from standard XCOM and you can  try it out for yourself on April 24th  it'll cost you just 10 US dollars when  it hits steam that day but the price  will go up to 20 on May 1st  stay tuned a GameSpot as we learn more  about the surprise new spinoff  [Music]
 

